  "full_prompt": "Create an animation explaining implicit differentiation. Start with a circle x² + y² = 25 and ask for the slope of the tangent line at point (3,4). Show that the curve is not a function (not y = f(x)). Introduce the idea of zooming in on the curve and considering tiny steps dx and dy. Define S = x² + y² as a function of two variables, and show that dS = 2x·dx + 2y·dy. Explain that staying on the circle means dS = 0, which gives the slope dy/dx = -x/y. Then show the ladder problem (related rates) as a parallel example where x and y are functions of time, with d(x²+y²)/dt = 0. Finally, use implicit differentiation to find the derivative of ln(x) by rewriting as e^y = x and differentiating both sides.",
